# refA_extra.py (deterministic)
== B2: Theorem 7.1, universal reading
  F = {~x0|x1, ~x1|x2, ~x2|x3, x0|~x1|x3}; every clause is an implicate of Ch_4: True
  prime implicates contained in the wide clause: only ~x1|x3 (x0 occurs positively and precedes x1)
  after replacement: edges {01,12,23,13}; UP_2-usable (= 2-hop TC-spanner): True
  F itself UP_2-usable: False
    UP_2 from {3: 0}: derived {1: 0, 2: 0, 3: 0}; entailed [(0, 0), (1, 0), (2, 0)]
    UP_2 from {0: 1}: derived {0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1}; entailed [(1, 1), (2, 1), (3, 1)]
== H: Prop 4.2(b), sound directed rules for one parity law (no auxiliaries)
  m=2: sound rules 12; with conclusion in the premise (trivial) 8; non-trivial with |P|=m-1: 4 (= m*2^(m-1) = 4)
  m=3: sound rules 54; with conclusion in the premise (trivial) 42; non-trivial with |P|=m-1: 12 (= m*2^(m-1) = 12)
  m=4: sound rules 216; with conclusion in the premise (trivial) 184; non-trivial with |P|=m-1: 32 (= m*2^(m-1) = 32)
  m=5: sound rules 810; with conclusion in the premise (trivial) 730; non-trivial with |P|=m-1: 80 (= m*2^(m-1) = 80)
